WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.720 --> 00:00:05.400
Which foods cause inflammation
and which foods reduce it?

00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:06.760
And why does it matter?

00:00:06.760 --> 00:00:09.281
That's what we'll be looking at
in this video and the next.

00:00:09.390 --> 00:00:20.201
"Foods That Cause Inflammation
and Those That Reduce It"

00:00:20.800 --> 00:00:24.720
Excessive inflammation may play a
role in a number of leading causes

00:00:24.720 --> 00:00:27.600
of death and disability,&nbsp;
including type 2 diabetes,

00:00:27.600 --> 00:00:29.680
obesity, and heart disease.

00:00:29.680 --> 00:00:31.760
But what are the stimuli that jumpstart

00:00:31.760 --> 00:00:34.560
the deleterious inﬂammatory cascade?

00:00:34.560 --> 00:00:37.040
You typically hear about
the pro-inflammatory nature

00:00:37.040 --> 00:00:41.280
of a chronic high-fat diet,
but the inflammatory effect

00:00:41.280 --> 00:00:44.280
“may not be limited to chronic
intake but may be evident

00:00:44.280 --> 00:00:47.600
after the consumption of a single meal.”

00:00:47.600 --> 00:00:51.400
Within hours after eating an
unhealthy meal, inflammatory markers

00:00:51.400 --> 00:00:58.520
like (IL-6), interleukin-6, can
skyrocket, doubling within six hours.

00:00:58.520 --> 00:01:00.880
The majority of studies show an increase in IL-6

00:01:00.880 --> 00:01:03.560
after the consumption of a high-fat meal.

00:01:03.560 --> 00:01:07.360
But the meals they tested weren’t
just filled with meat, eggs,

00:01:07.360 --> 00:01:10.440
dairy, and oil, but also junky refined carbs

00:01:10.440 --> 00:01:13.200
like white flour and added sugar.

00:01:13.200 --> 00:01:16.480
Yes, give people essentially
straight butter fat and no carbs,

00:01:16.480 --> 00:01:19.320
and you can still get a spike
in inflammation within hours,

00:01:19.320 --> 00:01:22.480
proving the added fat
itself is pro-inflammatory.

00:01:22.480 --> 00:01:26.080
But give people straight
sugar water without any fat,

00:01:26.080 --> 00:01:29.360
and you can get the same
thing, proving the added sugar

00:01:29.360 --> 00:01:33.360
is pro-inflammatory too.

00:01:33.360 --> 00:01:36.320
Why should we be concerned with
the inﬂammatory responses

00:01:36.320 --> 00:01:38.120
after unhealthy meal ingestion?

00:01:38.120 --> 00:01:41.200
Because substantial research
points to the notion that

00:01:41.200 --> 00:01:44.720
persistent low-grade inﬂammation
is an underlying factor

00:01:44.720 --> 00:01:47.560
in several high-mortality chronic
diseases, and that diet

00:01:47.560 --> 00:01:51.520
can contribute to, or
attenuate, that inﬂammation.

00:01:51.520 --> 00:01:56.960
You’ll note in this graph that IL-6
levels jumped up to about 3 pg/mL.

00:01:57.800 --> 00:02:00.680
You start regularly getting
up to levels of about 3 pg/mL,

00:02:00.680 --> 00:02:04.320
and that’s associated with
twice the risk of death.

00:02:04.320 --> 00:02:06.880
That increased risk was found across the board,

00:02:06.880 --> 00:02:09.640
compiling eight other similar
studies, likely because

00:02:09.640 --> 00:02:11.920
it’s linked with increased
risk of heart disease,

00:02:11.920 --> 00:02:15.200
the #1 killer of men and women,
even about as strongly as

00:02:15.200 --> 00:02:18.600
some other major established
risk factors like high cholesterol.

00:02:18.600 --> 00:02:22.280
Now, not all high-fat
foods cause inflammation.

00:02:22.280 --> 00:02:25.240
More than a dozen studies combined
show that whole plant foods

00:02:25.240 --> 00:02:28.680
such as nuts do not
increase inflammatory markers,

00:02:28.680 --> 00:02:31.560
even eating up to handfuls of nuts a day.

00:02:31.560 --> 00:02:34.160
In fact, spread half an
avocado on a beef burger,

00:02:34.160 --> 00:02:37.040
and you may be able to blunt
some of the inflammation

00:02:37.040 --> 00:02:40.760
caused by the meat—even lean meat.

00:02:40.760 --> 00:02:44.800
There are reviews purporting to show
a drop in inflammatory markers

00:02:44.800 --> 00:02:49.320
after eating wild game, which is
about as lean a meat as you can get,

00:02:49.320 --> 00:02:52.320
but that’s only compared
to store-bought meat.

00:02:52.320 --> 00:02:56.040
Give people some really fatty meat,
and their IL-6 shoots up,

00:02:56.040 --> 00:02:58.960
as does their tumor-necrosis
factor and C-reactive protein.

00:02:58.960 --> 00:03:01.120
Inflammatory, inflammatory, inflammatory

00:03:01.120 --> 00:03:03.520
within hours of it going into your mouth.

00:03:03.520 --> 00:03:06.480
But what if you instead
eat a kangaroo steak,

00:03:06.480 --> 00:03:09.720
extremely low fat on the
order of elk or moose?

00:03:09.720 --> 00:03:15.960
What you get is inflammatory,
inflammatory, inflammatory

00:03:15.960 --> 00:03:18.960
again within hours of it
going into your mouth.

00:03:18.960 --> 00:03:22.360
Now, certainly less inflammatory
than conventional meat

00:03:22.360 --> 00:03:25.480
you might get at the store, but
pro-inflammatory nonetheless,

00:03:25.480 --> 00:03:29.760
increasing markers of
inflammation within mere hours.

00:03:30.960 --> 00:03:33.960
“Intervention studies to
enhance healthy ageing need

00:03:33.960 --> 00:03:37.560
appropriate outcome measures,
such as blood-borne biomarkers,

00:03:37.560 --> 00:03:40.600
which are easily obtainable, cost-
effective, and widely accepted.”

00:03:40.600 --> 00:03:44.040
We need blood-borne
biomarkers of mortality risk.

00:03:44.040 --> 00:03:47.320
For example, having higher levels of
C-reactive protein in your blood

00:03:47.320 --> 00:03:52.240
ay increase your risk of dying
prematurely by 42 percent.

00:03:52.240 --> 00:03:55.800
C-reactive protein is the most
widely used inﬂammatory biomarker

00:03:55.800 --> 00:03:59.800
for predicting mortality, but those
with the highest levels of (IL-6),

00:03:59.800 --> 00:04:03.040
interleukin-6, another marker of
inflammation, may increase

00:04:03.040 --> 00:04:09.120
premature death risk 49 percent.
What can we do to bring it down?

00:04:09.120 --> 00:04:13.040
In my last video, I talked about
foods we eat that can contribute

00:04:13.040 --> 00:04:17.280
to inflammation like meat and sugar,
versus foods like nuts that don’t.

00:04:17.280 --> 00:04:19.440
But what about anti-inflammatory foods that

00:04:19.440 --> 00:04:22.520
actually attenuate that inflammation?

00:04:22.520 --> 00:04:24.480
Let’s see what happens
when you add blueberries

00:04:24.480 --> 00:04:26.960
to a high-fat meal with a high glycemic load.

00:04:26.960 --> 00:04:30.600
White potatoes, white bread, ham,
cheese, butter, and more cheese,

00:04:30.600 --> 00:04:33.560
with or without a single
cup of blueberries.

00:04:33.560 --> 00:04:38.680
Add blueberries and get a significant
drop in IL-6 from that meal.

00:04:38.680 --> 00:04:41.920
What about raspberries? Feed people
eggs, butter, white potatoes,

00:04:41.920 --> 00:04:44.560
white flour biscuits, and
sausage with or without two cups

00:04:44.560 --> 00:04:47.960
of frozen raspberries blended
with water into a smoothie,

00:04:47.960 --> 00:04:49.720
compared to giving people
the same amount

00:04:49.720 --> 00:04:52.840
of calories and carbs in banana form and...

00:04:52.840 --> 00:04:57.280
bananas were no match for the
meat, eggs, dairy, and crappy carbs;

00:04:57.280 --> 00:05:01.560
that resulted in a tripling of
IL-6 levels within four hours.

00:05:01.560 --> 00:05:04.640
But instead, drink those two cups of raspberries,

00:05:04.640 --> 00:05:07.680
and your body is able to hold the line.

00:05:07.680 --> 00:05:10.880
Why did raspberries work
whereas bananas didn’t?

00:05:10.880 --> 00:05:12.600
Maybe it’s the antioxidants?

00:05:12.600 --> 00:05:15.960
Well, antioxidant supplements failed miserably–

00:05:15.960 --> 00:05:18.360
no benefit from antioxidant vitamins and minerals

00:05:18.360 --> 00:05:21.880
like vitamins C, E, beta-
carotene, or selenium.

00:05:21.880 --> 00:05:26.280
Maybe it’s those special antioxidant
pigments, the anthocyanins

00:05:26.280 --> 00:05:29.320
that give berries those bright
red, blue, and purple colors?

00:05:29.320 --> 00:05:31.720
And indeed, that’s what
dozens of randomized

00:05:31.720 --> 00:05:33.840
controlled trials have demonstrated.

00:05:33.840 --> 00:05:36.120
Whereas a half dozen studies
combined show pomegranates,

00:05:36.120 --> 00:05:38.720
a fruit packed with anthocyanin pigments,

00:05:38.720 --> 00:05:42.080
can bring down inflammation over time.

00:05:42.080 --> 00:05:44.200
What about adding spices to meals

00:05:44.200 --> 00:05:46.680
as an approach to cool down inflammation?

00:05:46.680 --> 00:05:50.080
Supplementation with grape
and turmeric extracts did not

00:05:50.080 --> 00:05:52.240
affect the inflammatory
response to a milkshake.

00:05:52.240 --> 00:05:56.560
But give people actual turmeric,
one teaspoon a day of the whole spice,

00:05:56.560 --> 00:05:59.800
and you get a significant drop in IL-6 levels,

00:05:59.800 --> 00:06:03.920
but not when you just give people
purified curcumin supplements.

00:06:03.920 --> 00:06:06.480
Garlic powder reduced IL-6 levels as well,

00:06:06.480 --> 00:06:08.880
starting at about a half teaspoon a day.

00:06:08.880 --> 00:06:12.520
And ginger powder (just ground ginger)
showed the same thing,

00:06:12.520 --> 00:06:17.080
with doses ranging from half a
teaspoon to one and a half teaspoons.

00:06:17.080 --> 00:06:19.040
Of course, another way to
mediate the inflammation

00:06:19.040 --> 00:06:25.120
caused by a Sausage and Egg McMuffin
is to not eat it in the first place.

00:06:25.120 --> 00:06:27.400
What about just eating a plant-based diet?

00:06:27.400 --> 00:06:33.000
To my surprise, the drop in IL-6 did
not reach statistical significance.

00:06:33.000 --> 00:06:35.800
Whenever a dietary intervention
doesn’t have the result you expect,

00:06:35.800 --> 00:06:41.080
you always have to ask,
“What was the diet they exactly ate?”

00:06:41.080 --> 00:06:43.720
The study mostly looked
at the Mediterranean diet,

00:06:43.720 --> 00:06:45.480
which certainly has more plants,

00:06:45.480 --> 00:06:49.000
but maybe the diets didn’t go far enough?

00:06:49.000 --> 00:06:52.240
To figure that out, we can
turn to Dr. Turner-McGrievy’s

00:06:52.240 --> 00:06:56.360
famous New DIETs study where
people either continued to eat

00:06:56.360 --> 00:07:01.200
their fully omnivorous diets or
were randomized to eat a vegan diet,

00:07:01.200 --> 00:07:04.200
a vegetarian diet,
a pesco-vegetarian diet,

00:07:04.200 --> 00:07:06.000
or a semi-vegetarian diet that,

00:07:06.000 --> 00:07:08.280
for example, limited red meat.

00:07:08.280 --> 00:07:10.960
So, whereas the vegan might
eat red beans and brown rice

00:07:10.960 --> 00:07:13.440
with chopped tomatoes and
roasted peppers for dinner,

00:07:13.440 --> 00:07:16.320
the ovo-lacto-vegetarian
might add some cheese,

00:07:16.320 --> 00:07:18.920
the peso-vegetarian might add shrimp,

00:07:18.920 --> 00:07:22.280
and the semi-vegetarian might
have some turkey sausage.

00:07:22.280 --> 00:07:24.800
What happened within two months to their

00:07:24.800 --> 00:07:29.720
Dietary Inflammatory Index scores?
The Dietary Inflammatory Index

00:07:29.720 --> 00:07:32.800
is a measure of how
inflammatory your diet is.

00:07:32.800 --> 00:07:36.200
Negative scores mean your overall
diet is anti-inflammatory

00:07:36.200 --> 00:07:39.080
and the lower the better,
whereas positive scores mean

00:07:39.080 --> 00:07:41.320
your diet is on balance pro-inflammatory.

00:07:41.320 --> 00:07:44.880
And that’s exactly where
they all started out.

00:07:44.880 --> 00:07:47.000
No surprise, as they
were eating regular diets,

00:07:47.000 --> 00:07:51.480
and our nation is awash with
inflammation-related disease.

00:07:51.480 --> 00:07:54.080
But ask people to switch to
strictly plant-based nutrition,

00:07:54.080 --> 00:07:57.680
and their diet flips to become
an anti-inflammatory diet.

00:07:57.680 --> 00:08:00.640
And that was the case even
if they just cut out meat,

00:08:00.640 --> 00:08:03.120
or just all meat except fish.

00:08:03.120 --> 00:08:06.440
But have them instead switch mostly
to poultry, or simply limit their

00:08:06.440 --> 00:08:10.240
meat intake, and their
diet remains inflammatory.

00:08:10.240 --> 00:08:13.320
Now, not all plant-foods
are anti-inflammatory.

00:08:13.320 --> 00:08:16.120
If all you do is boost your intake
of less healthy plant foods,

00:08:16.120 --> 00:08:19.920
like juice, white bread, white
potatoes, soda, and cake

00:08:19.920 --> 00:08:22.040
you can end up even more inflamed.

00:08:22.040 --> 00:08:24.640
But if you eat a really clean
diet of whole plant foods,

00:08:24.640 --> 00:08:27.320
not only do you get a significant
reductions in Lp(a)

00:08:27.840 --> 00:08:30.080
(which we didn’t even think
was possible with diet),

00:08:30.080 --> 00:08:32.320
as well as drops in LDL cholesterol, of course,

00:08:32.320 --> 00:08:34.840
and even the most dangerous
form of LDL cholesterol,

00:08:34.840 --> 00:08:40.480
but nearly across the board you also
get a drop in inflammatory markers.

00:08:40.480 --> 00:08:43.200
We’re talking a 30 percent
drop in C-reactive protein,

00:08:43.200 --> 00:08:45.480
a 20 percent drop in IL-6.

00:08:45.480 --> 00:08:49.280
So, maybe previous studies
utilizing plant-centered diets

00:08:49.280 --> 00:08:52.440
were unsuccessful because they
weren’t plant-based enough,

00:08:52.440 --> 00:08:55.640
with animal products still being
substantially consumed.

00:08:55.640 --> 00:08:58.720
The total elimination of animal
products and processed foods

00:08:58.720 --> 00:09:05.683
may therefore be a more prudent dietary
strategy to combat inflammation.

